WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:17.825
The next morning at school, everyone was talking about the tornado.

2
00:00:17.826 --> 00:00:23.466
"It went right over Willow Creek!" exclaimed Carlos. "It was great!"

3
00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:27.329
"Oh, Carlos," said Katie, rolling her eyes.

4
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:31.161
"People aren't supposed to like tornados."

5
00:00:31.162 --> 00:00:36.696
"Well, I do," said Carlos.

6
00:00:36.697 --> 00:00:42.081
"Tell me about your family tornado safety teams," Mr. Higgins said.

7
00:00:42.082 --> 00:00:44.560
"Did you all have a plan?"

8
00:00:44.561 --> 00:00:49.790
"Katie was our captain," said Joy, smiling at her sister.

9
00:00:49.791 --> 00:00:53.194
"Everybody worked together," added Katie.

10
00:00:53.195 --> 00:00:56.295
"Mom and I made a first aid kit."

11
00:00:56.296 --> 00:01:00.217
"But luckily, we didn't need it," Joy said.

12
00:01:00.218 --> 00:01:05.433
"And Joy found Jellybean after the storm!" Katie announced.

13
00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:10.387
"Well, Dad and I did," said Joy shyly.

14
00:01:10.388 --> 00:01:14.513
"My house doesn't have a cellar," said Carlos.

15
00:01:14.514 --> 00:01:17.732
"So we decided that a hallway would be the safest place.

16
00:01:17.733 --> 00:01:20.080
There are no windows there."

17
00:01:20.081 --> 00:01:25.386
"Flying glass can be dangerous during a tornado," said Mr. Higgins.

18
00:01:25.387 --> 00:01:28.427
"What about your family, Luke?"

19
00:01:28.428 --> 00:01:32.421
"He forgot to make a plan," tattled Katie.

20
00:01:32.422 --> 00:01:35.244
Luke made a face at her.

21
00:01:35.245 --> 00:01:40.614
"I was at the coffee shop when we heard the tornado warning," he said.

22
00:01:40.615 --> 00:01:46.483
"Mom gave everyone a free fried pie and took them to the basement."

23
00:01:46.484 --> 00:01:52.051
"My dad actually saw the tornado," said Larry Ferguson.

24
00:01:52.052 --> 00:01:55.648
"We all went down into the storm cellar.

25
00:01:55.649 --> 00:02:00.097
But just before Dad shut the door, he looked up.

26
00:02:00.098 --> 00:02:03.980
The tornado was coming right across the field!

27
00:02:03.981 --> 00:02:08.144
Our barn went up in the air and crashed down hard.

28
00:02:08.145 --> 00:02:11.620
It broke into a hundred pieces."

29
00:02:11.621 --> 00:02:15.559
"Were there any cows in the barn?" asked Carlos.

30
00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:19.639
"No," said Larry, "just my bicycle.

31
00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:22.116
We haven't found it yet."

32
00:02:22.117 --> 00:02:27.355
"Larry, I'm sorry to hear your barn was destroyed," said Mr. Higgins.

33
00:02:27.356 --> 00:02:30.063
The class nodded.

34
00:02:30.064 --> 00:02:32.866
"Thank you," said Larry.

35
00:02:32.867 --> 00:02:35.676
"But our neighbors are coming over today.

36
00:02:35.677 --> 00:02:38.890
They're going to help Dad build a new barn."

37
00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:41.703
"That's great," said Mr. Higgins.

38
00:02:41.704 --> 00:02:45.035
"It's a big help when people work together."

39
00:02:45.036 --> 00:02:49.996
Then Mr. Higgins asked Larry what the tornado sounded like.

40
00:02:49.997 --> 00:02:52.171
Larry thought for a moment.

41
00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:55.376
"It sounded like . . . like a . . ."

42
00:02:55.377 --> 00:03:00.947
"Like a train!" said Katie. "Roar!"

43
00:03:00.948 --> 00:03:06.226
"It even whistled like a train!" said Joy. "Woo-woo!"

44
00:03:06.227 --> 00:03:12.195
"I think it sounded like a jet plane," said Carlos. "Varoom!"

45
00:03:12.196 --> 00:03:20.158
"It made a noise," said Laura, "like when we go fast in the car with the windows down. Whoosh!"

46
00:03:20.159 --> 00:03:26.367
"It was like a wild animal . . . a lion!" said Luke. "Grr!"

47
00:03:26.368 --> 00:03:36.058
Everybody started making scary sounds.

48
00:03:36.059 --> 00:03:39.767
"TAKE COVER!" cried Katie.

49
00:03:39.768 --> 00:03:43.303
That made everybody laugh.

50
00:03:43.304 --> 00:03:46.210
Suddenly Mr. Higgins waved his arms.

51
00:03:46.211 --> 00:03:50.817
"Quiet, please!" he called. "Quiet!"

52
00:03:50.818 --> 00:03:55.997
They heard a knock on the door, and Ms. Olson stepped into the classroom.

53
00:03:55.998 --> 00:03:58.104
She looked at Mr. Higgins.

54
00:03:58.105 --> 00:04:02.854
"I thought I heard a tornado as I came down the hall," she said.

55
00:04:02.855 --> 00:04:07.270
Everybody laughed again, and Ms. Olson smiled.

56
00:04:07.271 --> 00:04:10.274
"Mr. Higgins," she said.

57
00:04:10.275 --> 00:04:15.454
"The school yard is covered with tree branches that were blown down during the storm.

58
00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:19.426
Would your class like to help clean up the playground?"

59
00:04:19.427 --> 00:04:25.593
"Yes!" cried all the boys and girls. "We'll help!"

60
00:04:25.594 --> 00:04:31.301
So when recess came, Mr. Higgins led the class out to the playground.

61
00:04:31.302 --> 00:04:35.467
They gathered all the branches into a big pile.

62
00:04:35.468 --> 00:04:38.505
Mr. Higgins carried the heavy branches.

63
00:04:38.506 --> 00:04:42.159
Laura helped Joy carry a big branch.

64
00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:44.760
Carlos found one blue sneaker.

65
00:04:44.761 --> 00:04:49.255
Katie found a broken umbrella under the slide.

66
00:04:49.256 --> 00:04:52.909
Then the kids stood in front of their mountain of tree limbs.

67
00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:57.534
Ms. Olson took a photo.

68
00:04:57.535 --> 00:05:02.734
The next day, she put the photo on the bulletin board in the hall.

69
00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:12.393
Under the photo, she pinned up big letters that spelled "TEAMWORK WORKS!"
